ng  speaks up against him but flock just  shoots him and kills him he then uses  the  man is an example for the other  volunteers and tells them that there is  no reason for anyone else to die as long  as they obeyed the will of the glorious  King Emperor flock Forster the proud  owner of the most stylish bangs on  parody's Mikasa shows up and she and  Jean are like flock buddy are you ok man  what's going on with you at this point  flock sounds like some kind of crazy  zealot and he has taken it upon himself  to cleanse the island of hatred while  Aaron cleanses the rest of the world he  seems to think that after he gets rid of  everyone he doesn't like on the island  while Aaron gets rid of everyone off the  island then they will all finally be  free to live whichever way they want to  live I mean ok I can understand how  someone who grew up in that cruel world  and served as a soldier for all those  years could lose it like this but I'm  willing to bet that Aaron doesn't give a  damn about flock and he probably never  even told him his plan and let's face it  Aaron isn't the only one I bet that no  one out there watching or listening to  this right now literally no one gives a  damn about flock and if you see that one  guy in the comments saying flock is best  boy I love his best genius hairstyle and  so on you can be certain that they're  just memeing nobody loves flock nobody  moving on  Mikasa asks the legendary King Emperor  flock where han Jie and Levi are and he  tells them that they were both killed by  Zeke again definitely 100% not total BS  meanwhile falco is riding with Kony on  horseback Kony is telling Falco that he  lost his memory and Kony is just trying  to take him to the hospital although in  reality he wants to feed him to his  mother well I can appreciate a son  wanting to prepare a hot meal for his  mother every once in a while I think  corny will end up changing his mind  although he may not even get the chance  to change his mind because falco is  already thinking about somehow bitching  Kony and heading back south to meet up  with Gabi and the others as all of this  is happening and as you can see a lot is  happening in all sorts of different  locations at the same time we also see  Peake and McGrath watching the wall  Titans marched towards the sea as the  Marlin airships rushed back to the  continent the airships are trying to get  back and warn everyone about the  rumbling and Peake asks  if the Marlin military has any way to  stop Aaron magatha says no there's  really nothing that they can do except  hold out until the very end but then  suddenly the two of them are approached  by Han Jie han Jie puts her hands up and  tells them that she is unarmed she also  points to a wagon behind her where an  injured man is wrapped up in bandages  and lying down motionless han Jie says  that the man inside the cart is a  completely harmless man who failed to  die and the text on the final page says  that a soldier shall not die until he  has given meaning to his life just as I  thought and just as a lot of you thought  Levi is injured but he is indeed alive  there is no way that an absolute mad lad  like Levi would die in such a random and  off-screen way not after everything he's  been through how ironic is it that Han  Jie called them completely harmless  absolutely hilarious  it's true that this chapter didn't have  any epic Titan battles but it had a ton  of moving parts we saw a bunch of  different scenes playing out at  different locations at the same time  including a knee and hitch the audience  rebelling at Lee Barry Oh Armin and  Mikasa king-emperor flock Han Jie and  Levi so much is happening I feel like  all the chess pieces are being moved  into place before we get to the final  showdown although it is difficult to say  what precise form this final showdown  will take personally I am very happy  that Annie and Levi are back and call me  crazy but I predict that flock will not  make it to the end